2026-09-27T09:56:43.2529408Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2529787Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2530154Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2530927Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2531562Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2531631Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2531783Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2531998Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532194Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532262Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532430Z ================
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532522Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532638Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2532906Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533056Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533146Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533349Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533474Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533576Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2533838Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2534093Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2534579Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2535196Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2535285Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2535625Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2594446Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2594873Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2595220Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2595721Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2595826Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2596077Z ========
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2596244Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2597536Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2598923Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2599171Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2599692Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2600630Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2601270Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2601921Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2602457Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2602962Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2603083Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2603376Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2603554Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2604991Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2606392Z 
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2607154Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2608171Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:56:43.2608427Z 
